Z||000000||onfire||02-26-2001||04:06 AM||||I have a friend that works at a car rental place. She hooked me up with a 2001 Nissan Maxima for $56. I picked it up Thurs. night and I don't have to take it back til Mon. night. Unlimited mileage, and full coverage insurance. Anyway, I took my friend to Spokane to pick up his wife(visiting family). <P>  The cars cruise control will only engage upto 91 m.p.h. The speedometer goes upto 160, but it has a speed limiter at 130. Don't ask me how I know this.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I also took the car to the Ocean, and Mount St. Helens. All in all I put about 1300 miles on the car in about three days. Needless to say I got my money's worth. I hope she doesn't read this, she might not rent another car to me. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||02-26-2001||08:23 AM||||interesting. When I owned my Mercedes SL, they were loaded with all the options. Everything EXCEPT any cruise control. Mine was a european version with the aero headlites and small bumpers and figured it should have cruise for the autobahns. Anyway since mine was a factory AMG modified version I asked why it didnt have it. I was told it was a safety factor. AMG didnt want people on autobahn at 150+ MPH with cruise control engaged. Maybe thats why your rental had the limit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||02-26-2001||10:43 AM||||I believe safety would be the concern for not allowing the cruise to be on at high speeds.<P>I'm sort of curious if cars that tell you the outside temperature and display "ICE" in conditions are favorable for ICE.  Ah, will those cars let you turn on the cruise when it says ICE?<P>Also, last fall I had to make a panic stop with my dad's '89 Chevy pickup and I had the cruise on at about 55mph.  Off course as soon as I stabbed the brake it automatically shut the cruise off, but for some reason it would let me put the cruise back on.<P>The Windows, "shut down and restart" method got it to work again.  Does anyone know if the cruise is supposed to do this?<P>Sorry for the tangent...<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 02-26-2001).]||||reg||1
